1
00:00:00,693 --> 00:00:03,693
Hand-holding is only allowed
under the following circumstances.

2
00:00:03,905 --> 00:00:08,365
A, either party is in danger
of falling off a cliff, precipice or ledge.

3
00:00:08,535 --> 00:00:13,375
B, either party is deserving of a hearty
handshake after winning a Nobel Prize.

4
00:00:13,540 --> 00:00:17,000
C, moral support during flu shots."

5
00:00:19,712 --> 00:00:22,962
- Seems a bit restrictive.
- Yeah, well, feel free to retain a lawyer.

6
00:00:33,393 --> 00:00:35,313
Penny, I said, "Right hand, red."

7
00:00:35,478 --> 00:00:38,518
Yeah, I heard you. I got red. Ahem.

8
00:00:39,858 --> 00:00:41,738
(Amy:)Bernadette...

9
00:00:42,235 --> 00:00:44,275
(Amy:)...left foot, yellow.

10
00:00:46,114 --> 00:00:49,454
(Bernadette:)We should play limbo next.
No one beats me at limbo.

11
00:00:52,078 --> 00:00:55,578
Penny? Amy? Bernadette?

12
00:00:56,708 --> 00:00:57,838
(Amy:)That's my boyfriend.

13
00:00:58,001 --> 00:00:59,251
(Amy:)It's open.

14
00:01:00,587 --> 00:01:01,877
(Sheldon:)I got a splinter.

15
00:01:03,256 --> 00:01:04,926
(Amy:)What do you want me to do about it?

16
00:01:05,091 --> 00:01:07,761
(Sheldon:)Relationship Agreement
Section 4: Boo-boos and Ouchies.

17
00:01:07,927 --> 00:01:09,677
(Sheldon:)You have to take care of it.

18
00:01:10,555 --> 00:01:12,975
(Amy:)I should've gotten a lawyer.

19
00:01:15,768 --> 00:01:17,438
(Bernadette:)Looks like it's just us playing.

20
00:01:24,110 --> 00:01:25,990
(Bernadette:)Penny?

21
00:01:28,615 --> 00:01:32,285
- Penny, we're out of wine.
- You should probably drive.

